# state: first-run
# Need for Speed: Most Wanted (4541007B), lane.nfsroute1011 (10-11, #433 step 3): a profile
# route, not a measurement. Boots, creates and SAVES an alias ("ABCR"), leaves autosave on,
# reaches the main menu, then `mark profile-saved` and `flush` -- the only route this title's
# incoming dispatcher-level profile gate admits with no saved profile (brief addendum 2,
# lane.local 10-11 12:17 PDT: a `# state: first-run` route with no `mark profile-saved` is
# refused). No `mark gameplay`: this route never races.
#
# Boot timing (s01-s03) and the alias-create / autosave-notice dialogs (s04-s06) are the same
# screens nfs-mw-quickrace.route's own gated steps already cover, so this route reuses its refs
# (routes/refs/nfs-mw-quickrace/{alias-prompt,autosave-notice1,autosave-notice2,main-menu}.png)
# rather than duplicating them -- all four are name-independent and pass waitfor_match.py
# against this route's own frames at the same region/threshold (NOTES.md has the score table).
#
# What differs from nfs-mw-quickrace: that route's s07 (4x DOWN + 2x RIGHT from the keyboard's
# default cursor on "A") never types a letter, it only navigates straight to the footer's
# "Done" and submits the untouched "NAME" placeholder, which its s08 then DECLINES -- the
# owner's bug report ("stuck in a profile creation screen scrolling through keys and buttons")
# is this route never finishing the keyboard. This route's own s07 types a real name instead,
# letter by letter (A types the highlighted cell and the cursor stays on it; RIGHT/DOWN move
# exactly one grid cell, DOWN preserving the column until a narrower row -- Space, then the
# 3-cell footer -- collapses it), then s08 selects YES on the resulting save prompt. Both
# mechanics came from reading raw frames of a held pathfind.py session one at a time (not from
# guessing, per the brief's "find out from frames" on this exact keyboard):
# docs/lanes/nfsroute1011/scratch/pathfind-keyboard/frames/007-look.png is the keyboard's true
# default state (cursor on "A", field still reading the "NAME" placeholder); 008/009-look.png
# show A-types-and-stays plus DOWN-preserves-column, after actions "A RIGHT A RIGHT A" and
# "DOWN RIGHT RIGHT A" respectively; 010-look.png is the resulting "Do you want to save the
# alias ABCR?" prompt (No still default, same as nfs-mw-quickrace's s08); 012-look.png is the
# main menu reached afterward with the saved alias "ABCR" shown. This route's s07/s08 replay
# that exact, frame-verified action sequence (see NOTES.md for the full trace).
wait 13.3
shot s01-publisher_logo
press START 120
wait 0.6
wait 11.0
shot s02-intro_video
press START 120
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 10.4
shot s03-intro_video
press START 120
wait 0.6
wait 6.8
shot s04-alias_prompt
waitfor alias-prompt 20 160,195,970,460 5
# "Create a new alias?", No default (bracket box). One DOWN selects Yes.
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 7.9
shot s05-autosave_notice1
waitfor autosave-notice1 20 160,195,970,460 5
# Autosave-feature notice, single OK button.
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 7.3
shot s06-autosave_notice2
waitfor autosave-notice2 20 160,195,970,460 5
# "Do not remove controller..." notice, single OK button.
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 11.0
shot s07-name_entry
waitfor name-entry-cursor 30 230,345,230,60 5
# Keyboard opens on the "NAME" placeholder, cursor on letter A (row0,col0). Type "ABC":
# A (types A, cursor stays on it), RIGHT, A (types B), RIGHT, A (types C). Cursor now row0,col2.
press A 120
wait 0.6
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
# DOWN to row1,col2 ("P"), RIGHT RIGHT to row1,col4 ("R"); A types it. Field now "ABCR".
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 0.6
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 0.6
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
# DOWN x3 from row1,col4: digit row, Space (one wide cell), footer col0 ("Lowercase").
# RIGHT RIGHT to "Done" (footer col2). A submits "ABCR".
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 0.6
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 0.6
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 0.6
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 0.6
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 11.6
shot s08-alias_save_prompt
waitfor alias-save-prompt 30 160,195,970,460 10
# "Do you want to save the alias ABCR?", No still default (unlike nfs-mw-quickrace's s08,
# which declines here since its name was never typed). One DOWN selects Yes.
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 8.6
shot s09-saving
wait 11.5
shot s10-main_menu
waitfor main-menu 20 500,650,680,300 0.6
mark profile-saved
flush 20
